# interplay_memlive_held_cmdbuf: Command-buffer pages rewritten while their execs wait on the gate. Exec 1 (root FIFO) has its segment at VA page 4; exec 2 (worker FIFO, child 2, behind the same gate) has a 40-byte fill segment starting 36 bytes before VA page 6, so only its fill value and padding are in page 6; exec 3 (root FIFO) reads its segment at VA page 5, whose leaf the guest makes read-only. While they wait the guest points page 4's leaf at a page holding another segment and page 6's at a page holding another fill value. Each FIFO copied its command before the barrier, but a command buffer is walked when the exec runs: released, exec 1 runs the other segment, exec 2 runs a segment spliced from two pages (the first page's header and fill fields, the new page's value), and exec 3 runs from the read-only page (a command buffer is only read). The two FIFOs run at once after the gate opens, so the blocks setup's read_memory calls are reported sorted.
